UPDATE companies SET description='Island Pacific Distributors was founded on October 2, 1978 by Barbara and Leon Wolfley in Honolulu, Hawaii. The company began as a wholesale hardware and locksmith supply operation on King Street, serving the high-rise condominium boom in Waikiki and the Ala Wai corridor.

Today IPD operates from a 35,000-square-foot facility on Alakawa Street that houses offices, a warehouse, a showroom, and a steel door and frame fabrication shop staffed by two certified welders. The shop holds the state''s only Warnock Hersey Mark certification from Intertek for constructing and modifying Assa Abloy''s Curries line of hollow metal doors and frames. The company distributes doors, frames, finish hardware, security products, and specialty building products, and provides consultation, design, specification writing, installation, maintenance, electronic access control, and locksmith services. It has completed hundreds of projects and distributed millions of products across the islands.

IPD serves architects, general contractors, facility owners, and management companies in Hawaii''s hospitality, commercial construction, government, luxury residential, and condominium sectors. Notable projects include the Allure Waikiki, Moana Surfrider, Sheraton Moana Surfrider, Four Seasons Resort Lanai, Disney Aulani Resort, Kapolei Judiciary Complex, and Kamehameha Schools.

The company''s "Find A Way" motto reflects its commitment to customer service and problem-solving. Its differentiators include being Hawaii''s only certified Architectural Hardware Consultant, exclusive distributor for Sargent Hardware, Smoke Guard, CornellCookson, and Total Door Openings System, and an employee-owned structure that aligns staff incentives with long-term client relationships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Architectural hardware distribution", "Consultation and analysis", "Design and drawing (electronic)", "Specification and technical writing", "Installation of doors, hardware, expansion joints, overhead coiling doors/grilles, integrated door systems, electronic access control", "Maintenance and service", "Electronic access control solutions (consultation, design, installation, tech support)", "In-house locksmith (key cutting, rekeying, master keying)", "Steel door fabrication (hollow metal doors and frames, certified welders, Warnock Hersey labeling)", "Project management", "Specialty systems design"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Commercial construction", "Government facilities", "Luxury residential", "Condominium construction", "Education", "Federal facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Warnock Hersey Mark shop (Intertek certified) for hollow metal door/frame fabrication", "Intertek Testing Services (ITS) / Warnock Hersey (WHI) file labeling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hawaii''s only certified Architectural Hardware Consultant", "Only Warnock Hersey Mark shop in the state certified by Intertek for Assa Abloy Curries hollow metal doors and frames", "Exclusive Hawaii distributor for Sargent Hardware, Smoke Guard, CornellCookson, and Total Door Openings System", "Employee-owned (ESOP) since 2014 with staff averaging nearly 20 years tenure", "In-house locksmith and steel door fabrication with certified welders"], "facts_used": ["Founded October 2, 1978 by Barbara and Leon Wolfley -> /about", "Started as Wholesale Hardware and Locksmith Supply Company at King Street -> /about", "Employee-owned (ESOP) since 2014 -> /about", "Facility: 35,000 sq ft on Alakawa Street with offices, warehouse, showroom, steel door/frame fabrication shop -> /about", "Two certified welders, Warnock Hersey Mark shop certified by Intertek for Assa Abloy Curries line -> /about, /services", "Exclusive Hawaii distributor for Sargent Hardware, Smoke Guard, CornellCookson, Total Door Openings System -> /about", "Completed hundreds of projects, distributed millions of products -> /", "Projects: Allure Waikiki, Moana Surfrider, Sheraton Moana Surfrider, Four Seasons Resort Lanai, Disney Aulani Resort, Kapolei Judiciary Complex, Kamehameha Schools -> /", "Services: consultation, design, specification writing, installation, maintenance, electronic access control, locksmith, steel door fabrication -> /services", "Hawaii''s only certified Architectural Hardware Consultant -> /services", "In-house locksmith with key cutting, rekeying, master keying -> /services", "Steel door fabrication with certified welders, licensed by Intertek/Warnock Hersey for file labeling -> /services", "Motto \"Find A Way\" -> /about", "Staff averaging nearly 20 years tenure -> /about", "Purchased warehouse in 2021 for weld shop, installation teams -> /about", "Leadership: Kim Conner and Robert Field -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Island Pacific Distributors is the leading distributor of doors, frames, finish hardware, security products, and specialty building products in the Hawaiian islands.", "founded_year": "1978", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='island-pacific-distributors' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J & O Plastics operates from a 250,000-square-foot facility in Rittman, Ohio, a location chosen for its access to the northern Ohio retail distribution corridor. The company was founded in 1982 by Oscar and Christine Gross, initially supplying injection-molded parts to the Mr. Coffee Company.

The core operation is custom plastic injection molding, with a specialty in clear resins. J & O is one of the few U.S. molders running a proprietary process for straight PET, a BPA-free, low-cost clear plastic, alongside acrylic, polypropylene, SAN, crystal styrene, PVC, ABS, LDPE, and HDPE. The plant handles large-part molding and provides in-line assembly, kitting, packaging, barcoding, warehousing, inventory management, and direct shipment to major retailers.

Customers span household goods, industrial, agricultural, medical, and shipping/logistics sectors. The company is certified to ship directly to Amazon FBA, Costco, Walmart, Target, and Bed Bath & Beyond, handling SKU management, UPC barcoding, and bulk packaging for those accounts. It also serves OEM industrial applications requiring precision-molded components.

The founders’ early focus on PET was driven by demand for durable, BPA-free clear products. That proprietary PET process, combined with automation, allows competitive pricing. A sustainability pledge keeps scrap below 1 percent, with all waste either resold or recycled, and cardboard baled daily for recycling.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Large part injection molding", "Clear resin injection molding (PET, acrylic, polypropylene, SAN, crystal styrene, PVC, ABS, LDPE, HDPE)", "In-line assembly", "Kitting", "Packaging", "Barcoding", "Warehousing", "Inventory management", "Direct shipment to retailers", "SKU management", "UPC barcoding", "Bulk packaging", "Logistics support", "Agricultural plastic molding", "Medical plastic molding", "Household product molding", "Industrial plastic molding"], "industries": ["Household products", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Medical", "Shipping & logistics containers", "OEM industrial"], "materials": ["PET", "Acrylic", "Polypropylene", "SAN", "Crystal Styrene", "PVC", "ABS", "LDPE", "HDPE"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping and delivery", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary straight PET injection molding for BPA-free clear parts", "Certified direct-ship supplier to Amazon FBA, Costco, Walmart, Target, Bed Bath & Beyond", "In-line assembly, kitting, packaging, barcoding, warehousing, and inventory management", "250,000 sq ft facility in Ohio\u2019s retail distribution corridor", "Scrap rate under 1% with full recycling of waste and cardboard"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1982 by Oscar and Christine Gross -> /about-us", "Began as injection molding supplier to Mr. Coffee Company -> /about-us", "Facility encompasses 250,000 square feet of production and warehousing -> /about-us", "Pioneered injection molding of straight PET -> /about-us", "Certified to direct ship to Amazon FBA, Costco, Walmart, Target, Bed Bath & Beyond -> /about-us", "Materials: PET, acrylic, polypropylene, SAN, crystal styrene, PVC, ABS, LDPE, HDPE -> / and /about-us", "Services: in-line assembly, kitting, packaging, barcoding, warehousing, inventory management, direct shipment -> /about-us", "Industries: household products, industrial, agricultural, medical, shipping & logistics -> / and /about-us", "Same-day shipping and delivery -> /about-us", "Scrap under 1%, recycling program -> /about-us", "Headquarters: Rittman, Ohio -> db and /about-us", "Founded year: 1982 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "J&O Plastics has been a leader in the plastic injection molding industry since 1982.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-o-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J & R Senior Sheetmetal, Inc. operates from Westerly, Rhode Island, as a family-owned business now in its third generation. The company traces its roots to over 40 years of roofing expertise and three decades of metalworking experience, though a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed. It began as a specialist in custom copper work for the coastal communities of Rhode Island, including Block Island.

The shop fabricates a range of sheet metal components for roofing and flashing applications. Core products include copper roof vents, wall vents, drip edges, valleys, window and door pans, shower pans, step flashing, chimney caps, scuppers, and radius flashing, all produced in 16-ounce copper and Freedom Gray zinc-copper alloy. The company also works in .032-inch painted aluminum for drip edges, drip caps, valleys, and step flashing. Beyond custom fabrication, J & R Senior Sheetmetal assembles standing seam roof bundles that package high-temperature ice-and-water shield, wall flashings, panels, clips, screws, Z-bar, and ridge caps. It also acts as a distributor for Wuko hand tools and PREFA roofing systems.

The customer base centers on residential builders, roofing contractors, and homeowners throughout Rhode Island, with a focus on the challenges of coastal construction. The company''s work is tailored to withstand New England weather, and its portfolio includes standing seam roofs, flat-pounded roofing, cupolas, chimney through-flashings, and radius roofs.

J & R Senior Sheetmetal emphasizes domestic production, noting that its products are made in the USA using a mix of antique hand tools and modern machinery. The firm highlights quick turnaround times and a collaborative approach with builders and roofers to address the unique demands of seaside architecture.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom copper fabrication", "Roof vent fabrication", "Wall vent fabrication", "Drip edge fabrication", "Custom metal roofing", "Standing seam roof installation", "Flat-pounded roofing", "Cupola fabrication", "Chimney through-flashing", "Radius roof fabrication", "Specialized .032 aluminum standing seam", "Standing seam roof bundle assembly", "Distribution of Wuko tools", "Distribution of PREFA products"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Roofing", "Coastal construction", "Home building"], "materials": ["Copper", "16oz copper", "Freedom Gray (zinc copper)", ".032 aluminum", ".032 painted aluminum"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Products made in the USA using antique hand tools and modern machinery", "Quick turnaround times on custom copper and aluminum fabrications", "Family-owned with three generations of metalworking experience", "Distributor for Wuko tools and PREFA roofing systems", "Specializes in coastal roofing solutions for New England weather"], "facts_used": ["Location: Westerly, Rhode Island -> db", "Family-owned and operated across three generations -> db", "Over 40 years roofing expertise, 30 years metal experience -> db", "Specializes in custom copper work -> db", "Serves most of Rhode Island including Block Island -> db", "Products: copper roof vents, wall vents, drip edges, valleys, window/door pans, shower pans, step flashing, chimney caps, scuppers, radius flashing -> /", "Materials: 16oz copper, Freedom Gray (zinc copper), .032 painted aluminum -> /", "Services: standing seam roof, flat pounded, cupola, chimney through flashing, radius roof, specialized .032 aluminum standing seam -> /", "Standing seam roof bundles with components -> /", "Distributor for Wuko tools and PREFA products -> /", "Made in USA using antique hand tools and modern machines -> /", "Quick turnaround times -> /", "Focus on coastal homes and New England weather -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom flashings, roof vents, wall vents, drip edges, and custom metal roofing", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-r-senior-sheetmetal-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J.E. Fifer Sheet Metal Fabricators operates from a 30,000-square-foot facility in Richmond, Virginia. The family-owned company was founded in 1986 by James and Judy Fifer and is now led by their son, Jason T. Fifer, as president.

The shop provides precision sheet metal fabrication and machining services, including CNC laser cutting, punching, bending, TIG/MIG welding (aluminum, stainless, and mild steel), CNC PEM insertion, saw cutting, rolling, shearing up to 10 feet by 1/4 inch, and deburring with a Costa Metal Finishing machine. It also runs CNC and manual mills and lathes for precision machining, builds custom machinery and replacement parts, and operates proprietary shrink-packaging equipment under the same roof.

The company emphasizes on-time delivery and repeat business as the cornerstone of its success.

Leadership frames the mission around “ever-increasing satisfaction and sustainability through leadership, consistency, and integrity,” achieved by continual quality improvement driven by customer and associate engagement.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet Metal Fabrication", "CNC Laser Cutting", "CNC Punching", "CNC Bending", "Welding (TIG, MIG: Aluminum, Stainless Steel, Mild Steel)", "CNC PEM Insertion", "Saw Cutting", "Rolling", "Shearing (10'' x 1/4\" mild steel)", "Deburring (Costa Metal Finishing)", "Precision Machining (CNC & Manual Mills & Lathes)", "Custom Machinery Manufacturing", "Replacement Parts Manufacturing", "Shrink Packaging", "Equipment/Machinery Upgrades"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless Steel", "Mild Steel"], "equipment": ["CNC Laser Cutting machine", "CNC Punching machine", "CNC Bending machine", "CNC PEM Insertion machine", "Costa Metal Finishing deburring machine", "CNC Mills", "Manual Mills", "CNC Lathes", "Manual Lathes", "Shrink packaging equipment", "Shear (10'' capacity)", "Rolling equipment", "Saw cutting equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30,000+ sq. ft. facility with state-of-the-art equipment", "In-house shrink-packaging equipment for combined fabrication and packaging", "Family-owned since 1986 with second-generation leadership", "Commitment to on-time delivery and timely communication", "Continual quality improvement through customer and associate engagement"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1986 by James and Judy Fifer -> /about", "Family-owned business -> /about", "30,000+ sq.ft. facility in Richmond, VA -> /about", "President Jason T. Fifer -> /about", "Services: CNC laser cutting, punching, bending, welding, PEM insertion, saw cutting, rolling, shearing, deburring -> /about and /", "Precision machining (CNC & manual mills & lathes) -> /about and /", "Custom machinery manufacturing and replacement parts -> /about and /", "Shrink packaging equipment in-house -> /about", "Mission statement on satisfaction, sustainability, leadership, consistency, integrity -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Fifer Sheet Metal is a precision fabricator of custom sheet metal parts and assemblies.", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-e-fifer-sheet-metal-fabricators-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J Hunter Woodworks operates from a showroom and workshop in Haddonfield, New Jersey. The business was founded by Jeremy Hunter, who serves as owner and master craftsman. Hunter brought 12 years of woodworking experience to the venture, driven by a passion for design and building purposeful spaces that turn a house into a home.

The shop produces custom furniture and built‑ins, including dining tables, breakfast nooks, credenzas, bookshelves, and cabinetry. Each piece is handcrafted from high‑quality, locally sourced wood. At the new Haddonfield location, clients can participate in on‑site table building, selecting handmade legs and custom tops to see their design take shape. The operation also offers free design consultations and works from client ideas or inspiration images.

The company serves residential customers and interior designers seeking one‑of‑a‑kind pieces, as well as corporate clients for commercial projects. Testimonials highlight projects such as a custom breakfast nook with storage drawers and upholstered cushions, a dining table designed to store in the floor, and a mantle matching existing woodwork.

Hunter emphasizes a collaborative design process, inviting customers to be part of the creation from concept to delivery. The combination of locally sourced materials, handcrafted construction, and an on‑site building experience distinguishes the shop in the custom woodworking market.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture making", "Custom built-ins", "Cabinetry", "Table making (dining tables, breakfast nooks)", "Credenza construction", "Bookshelf building", "Custom upholstery (cushions)", "Design consultation", "On-site assembly and building"], "industries": ["Residential", "Interior design", "Corporate"], "materials": ["Locally sourced wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["On-site custom table building at Haddonfield showroom", "Handcrafted by master craftsman Jeremy Hunter", "High-quality, locally sourced wood", "Free design consultations", "Collaborative design process from concept to delivery"], "facts_used": ["Location: Haddonfield, NJ -> db", "Founder: Jeremy Hunter -> /about", "12 years woodworking experience -> /about", "Products: custom furniture, built-ins, cabinets, tables, credenzas, bookshelves -> /", "Materials: high quality locally sourced wood -> /", "Handcrafted by master craftsman Jeremy Hunter -> /", "Serves interior designers and individuals -> /", "Corporate clients mentioned -> /", "On-site custom table building at new Haddonfield location -> /", "Free design consultations -> /", "Passion for design and building purposeful spaces -> /about", "Collaborative design process -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Each piece is hand crafted by master-craftsman Jeremy Hunter.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-hunter-woodworks' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JR Plastics & Machining, Inc. operates from Lowesville, Virginia, in the Blue Ridge Mountains about 25 miles south of Charlottesville. The business traces its roots to 1994 when it began as a custom vacuum forming firm. In 1998 the owners, David Trent and Raymond Schneider, incorporated the company and added a full CNC machine shop, enabling them to produce molds and secondary processes in-house. The two owners remain the primary contacts for every project.

The shop provides custom vacuum forming, hotwire bending, and CNC machining under one roof. Vacuum forming capacity reaches 24 by 50 inches with a 9-inch draw depth in plastics up to 0.250 inch thick, including PETG, PVC, ABS, polycarbonate (Kydex), polystyrene, acrylic, and HDPE. CNC machining handles parts up to 50 by 100 by 9 inches in aluminum, brass, and stainless steel. Equipment includes HAAS mills, lathes, and routers, plus custom-built forming and bending machines that the team maintains themselves to minimize downtime.

Customers span medical, electronics, food packaging, and sports performance sectors across North America. The company works directly with clients from prototype through large-scale production runs, offering engineering support to refine designs for cost and performance.

The firm differentiates itself by keeping the entire production process — mold making, forming, machining, and finishing — in a single facility, with an owner serving as the direct point of contact. Over 100 years of combined experience in vacuum forming, pressure forming, hotwire bending, and CNC programming underpins their ability to deliver quick turnaround on tooling and parts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom vacuum forming", "Hotwire bending", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "CNC routing", "In-house mold making", "Engineering and design assistance", "Prototyping", "Small-run production", "Large-scale production runs"], "industries": ["Medical", "Electronics", "Food packaging", "Sports performance"], "materials": ["PETG", "PVC", "ABS", "Polycarbonate (Kydex)", "Polystyrene", "Acrylic", "HDPE", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Stainless steel"], "equipment": ["HAAS mills", "HAAS lathes", "HAAS routers", "Custom-built vacuum forming equipment", "Custom-built hotwire bending equipment"], "volume": "Prototype to large-scale production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Entire production process under one roof (vacuum forming, CNC machining, mold making)", "Direct owner contact (David Trent or Raymond Schneider) from start to finish", "In-house custom forming and bending equipment built and maintained by the team", "Over 100 years collective experience in vacuum forming, hotwire bending, and CNC machining", "Engineering services to optimize design for performance and cost"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1994 as custom vacuum forming firm -> /", "Incorporated as JR Plastics & Machining, Inc. in 1998 with CNC machine shop -> /", "Owners: David Trent and Raymond Schneider -> /", "Location: Lowesville, VA -> /", "Vacuum forming capacity: 24\" x 50\" x 9\" deep, plastics up to 0.250\" thick -> /", "Materials for vacuum forming: PETG, PVC, ABS, Polycarbonate Kydex, Polystyrene, Acrylic, HDPE -> /", "CNC machining capacity: 50\" x 100\" x 9\" thick in aluminum, brass, stainless steel -> /", "Equipment: HAAS mills, lathes, routers; custom-built forming and bending equipment -> /", "Industries served: medical, electronics, food packaging, sports performance -> /", "Over 100 years collective experience; Raymond Schneider 50+ years in vacuum forming, pressure forming, hotwire bending; 40 years machining, programming, jig fixture design -> /", "Engineering services offered to improve design and save money -> /", "Direct owner contact for each project -> /", "Entire production process under one roof -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our services include custom vacuum forming, hotwire bending, and CNC machining.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-r-plastics-and-machining' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J&L Plastic Molding operates from Wallingford, Connecticut, where it runs a dedicated injection molding facility. The company focuses on transitioning molding projects from development into full-scale production, offering prototype and production tooling, injection molding, and insert molding.

Its core services include prototype and production tooling, injection molding, insert molding, and tool transfer. The shop occupies two buildings housing 28 injection molding machines with clamp forces from 28 to 385 tons and shot capacities of 0.6 to 24 ounces, enabling a range of part sizes and volumes. The facility is geared for both prototype and production runs.

The company primarily serves medical device manufacturers. A notable customer is LeMaitre Vascular, which recognized J&L as its Supplier of the Year for quality, delivery, innovation, and collaboration. J&L''s ISO 13485:2016 certification underscores its focus on medical-grade quality.

J&L emphasizes its expertise with engineered thermoplastic resins such as PEEK (Victrex), PEI (Ultem), PPSU (Radel), PPS (Ryton), LCP (Vectra), TPU, TPE, polycarbonate, and ABS. Its quality management system is certified to ISO 13485:2016 by NQA, supporting medical-grade production requirements.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "Prototype tooling", "Production tooling", "Insert molding", "Tool transfer", "Medical device molding", "Engineered thermoplastic processing"], "industries": ["Medical Device"], "materials": ["PPSU (Radel)", "PEI (Ultem)", "PEEK (Victrex)", "PPS (Ryton)", "LCP (Vectra)", "TPU", "TPE", "Polycarbonate", "ABS"], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (28\u2013385 ton clamp force)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 13485:2016 certified for medical device manufacturing", "Tool transfer process for moving existing tooling into production", "Expertise in engineered thermoplastics including PEEK, Ultem, Radel, and other high-performance resins", "28 injection molding machines (28\u2013385 ton clamp force) across two facilities"], "facts_used": ["Location: Wallingford, Connecticut -> db", "Certification: ISO 13485:2016 -> db", "Facility: two buildings, 28 injection molding machines (28-385 tons) -> /", "Processes: prototype tooling, production tooling, injection molding, insert molding, tool transfer -> /", "Industries: Medical Device manufacturers -> /", "Materials: PPSU, PEI, PEEK, PPS, LCP, TPU, TPE, Polycarbonate, ABS -> /", "Award: Supplier of the Year by LeMaitre Vascular -> /", "Quality system certified by NQA -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our Connecticut molding facility will supply all your production requirements and needs. We operate in two buildings in Wallingford, Connecticut with 28 injection molding machines ranging from 28 to 385 tons of clamp force.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-l-plastic-molding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J-Tech Construction & Solar was founded in 2004 in Lincoln, Nebraska. The company began as a roofing contractor and has operated continuously in the Lincoln and Grand Island areas for over two decades.

The firm provides a full range of exterior services for residential and commercial properties, including roofing (asphalt, metal, storm damage restoration), siding (seamless steel, metal, James Hardie fiber cement, vinyl), windows, doors, gutter systems, and solar panel installation. A distinguishing feature is its in-house metal fabrication capability, producing custom metal roofing and siding components for each project rather than relying on pre-manufactured panels. The company also employs drone technology for roof assessments.

J-Tech serves homeowners and commercial building owners across Nebraska (excluding the panhandle) and parts of Iowa, Kansas, South Dakota, and Missouri. Its customer base includes property owners in Lincoln, Omaha, Grand Island, Kearney, Hastings, and surrounding communities seeking roofing, siding, window, door, gutter, and solar solutions. The company works with insurance restoration projects as well.

The company emphasizes several differentiators: single-contractor accountability for all exterior trades without subcontractors, drone inspections that document conditions before work begins, certified installer status with ProVia and James Hardie, a Nebraska contractor registration, warranty-backed installations, free inspections and estimates, and financing options for large projects.', certifications=ARRAY['ProVia Partner (through Window Depot USA)','James Hardie Contractor Alliance Partner','Nebraska Contractor Registration #36130-25']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential roofing", "Commercial roofing", "Metal roofing", "Storm damage restoration", "Emergency roof tarping", "Seamless steel siding installation", "Metal siding installation", "Door installation", "Window installation", "Seamless gutter systems", "Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar panel installation", "In-house metal fabrication", "Drone roof inspections", "Insurance restoration"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Solar energy installation", "Roofing", "Exterior remodeling"], "materials": ["Asphalt shingles", "Metal (fabricated in-house)", "James Hardie fiber cement", "Vinyl siding"], "equipment": ["Drone inspection technology"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house metal fabrication for custom-fit roofing and siding components", "Drone-based roof inspections provided before any work begins", "All exterior trades (roofing, siding, windows, doors, gutters, solar) performed by one crew without subcontractors", "Over 20 years of continuous operation in Nebraska communities", "Certified partnerships with ProVia and James Hardie"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2004 -> db", "Headquarters Lincoln, Nebraska -> db", "In-house metal fabrication -> /", "Drone roof inspections -> /", "Full exterior services (roofing, siding, windows, doors, gutters, solar) -> /", "Service area: Nebraska (excl. panhandle), parts of IA, KS, SD, MO -> /", "ProVia Partner certification -> /", "James Hardie Contractor Alliance Partner -> /", "Nebraska Contractor Registration #36130-25 -> /", "Materials: asphalt shingles, metal, James Hardie fiber cement, vinyl siding -> /", "20+ years in business -> /", "Warranty-backed work -> /", "Free inspections and estimates -> /", "Financing available -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We fabricate our own metal components in-house for every project", "founded_year": "2004", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-tech-construction-and-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Minneapolis, Minnesota, J. Holtz Furniture operates as a solo studio where the proprietor designs and builds each piece individually. The business does not disclose a founding year, but the owner describes a commission process that begins with an initial consultation and progresses through sketches, scale drawings, and a deposit before scheduling.

The shop produces custom furniture, built-in cabinetry, doors, and architectural millwork, along with prototype parts for other companies. Every order is built one at a time using hand-selected hardwoods sourced locally when possible, and each piece receives a hand-rubbed finish. The maker draws on Shaker, Scandinavian, Mid Century Modern, and Asian woodworking traditions.

Clients include residential customers seeking unique furniture and built-ins, as well as other businesses that commission prototype work. The studio does not list specific industry sectors beyond custom woodworking and prototyping.

