UPDATE companies SET description='JMH Woodcraft Inc. was founded in 1926 in New York City. The company has operated continuously as a custom carpentry and cabinetmaking shop serving both residential and commercial clients across the city.

The shop produces custom woodwork including kitchen islands, built-in bookcases, radiator covers, wall units, entertainment centers, and custom cabinets. Its services extend to stain matching, customized molding, antique restoration, total design integration, expert installation, and painting and repair.

JMH Woodcraft serves a mix of institutional, commercial, and residential customers. Notable commercial and institutional projects include work for Mount Sinai School of Medicine, Christ and St. Stephens Church, V&T''s Restaurant, Firehouse Restaurant, Manhattan School for Children, Booker T. Washington Jr. High School, Beacon High School, and The Hungarian Pastry Shop. These references span healthcare, education, religious, and hospitality sectors.

