UPDATE companies SET description='JMW Fabrication was founded in 2003 in Quakertown, Pennsylvania. The company operates a full in-house fabrication shop and a mobile welding unit, serving customers across eastern Pennsylvania and New Jersey.

The shop provides certified metal fabrication and repair, working with steel, stainless steel, aluminum, cast iron, and cast steel. Core processes include CNC plasma cutting, press braking, punching, shearing, metal forming, automated cold saw cutting, and SMAW, GMAW, and GTAW welding. Equipment includes a CNC plasma table, press brake, iron worker, and automatic cutting saws, which the company says can handle thousands of pieces per day for small, medium, and large production runs. Output ranges from one-off prototypes and custom architectural pieces — such as floating stairs and modern railings — to structural components and production parts.

JMW serves commercial, industrial, and residential clients, with projects spanning structural steel, architectural metalwork, stairs, railings, and equipment repair. The mobile welding rig brings on-site capability, including propane-powered units for indoor work where air quality is a concern. Welders hold American Welding Society certifications for D1.1 structural steel and D1.3 and D9.1 sheet metal across steel, stainless, and aluminum.

The company states its differentiators are quality craftsmanship, planning, communication, and diligence, with a focus on delivering projects right the first time. All major equipment is American-made, and the firm prioritizes buying from local suppliers when possible.', certifications=ARRAY['AWS D1.1','AWS D1.3','AWS D9.1']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC plasma cutting", "Press brake forming", "Punching and shearing", "Metal forming", "Automated cold saw cutting", "Mobile welding", "SMAW (Stick) welding", "GMAW (MIG) welding", "GTAW (TIG) welding", "Structural steel fabrication", "Architectural metal fabrication", "Stair fabrication", "Railing fabrication", "Repair welding", "Production piece manufacturing", "Prototyping"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Industrial manufacturing", "Residential construction", "Structural steel", "Architectural metalwork", "Equipment repair"], "materials": ["Steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Cast iron", "Cast steel"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma table", "Press brake", "Iron worker", "Automatic cutting saws", "Mobile welding rig", "Propane-powered mobile welders"], "volume": "Small to large production runs, thousands of pieces per day", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AWS-certified welders (D1.1, D1.3, D9.1)", "Mobile welding with propane-powered rigs for indoor air quality", "In-house CNC plasma table, press brake, iron worker, and automatic cutting saws", "American-made equipment and preference for local sourcing", "Customer-retention focus over transactional jobs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 -> db", "Headquarters Quakertown, PA -> db", "Mobile welding and in-house fabrication -> /", "Certified welders AWS D1.1, D1.3, D9.1 -> /", "CNC plasma table, press brake, iron worker, automatic cutting saws -> /", "Materials: steel, stainless steel, aluminum, cast iron, cast steel -> /", "Serves Eastern PA and New Jersey -> /", "Business model: acquire and serve good customers -> /", "American-made equipment -> /", "Production capacity thousands of pieces per day -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We offer a full in-house fabrication shop and mobile welding to serve your needs.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jmw-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JPM Steel Fabrication was founded in 2010 in Bella Vista, Arkansas, as a veteran-owned small business (VOSB) and family-operated company. The founder, James P. McGary, an Army veteran who served in Iraq from 2003 to 2005, returned to his home region after a career in construction and concrete work. He recognized a shortage of skilled steel fabrication tradesmen in Northwest Arkansas and opened a shop with a single crew focused on storage solutions.

The company designs, fabricates, installs, maintains, repairs, and retrofits custom tension fabric storage buildings for bulk material storage. It also produces consumer products such as steel benches and fire pits, provides general contracting services for municipalities, and executes large-scale commercial customizations. From its Bella Vista facility, JPM employs multiple full-time steel fabricators, installation specialists, and office staff, serving customers across the continental United States. All buildings are engineer-approved and carry a 25-year warranty, with the first two years of maintenance included.

JPM serves agriculture (grain, hay, equipment storage), government and municipalities (salt, sand, maintenance buildings), waste and recycling, aviation (aircraft hangars), mining, equestrian facilities, port and intermodal transport, and railroad transportation.

