UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Fort Wayne, Indiana, KDA Furniture & Interiors is a woman- and veteran-owned business that has operated for over 40 years. Nicole Kenefic, a Purdue University Fort Wayne graduate in Commercial Interior Design (2003), has been with the company since 2003 and, along with her husband Brian, acquired RMK Design Associates in July 2018.

The company designs and hand-builds custom furniture, employing skilled craftsmen for woodworking, laminating, and finishing. Each piece is fabricated to client specifications using floor plans, then packaged, delivered, and installed by the same team that built it. The staff includes furniture artisans, NCIDQ-accredited designers, and installation specialists who have executed projects nationwide.

KDA serves healthcare, educational, financial, restaurant, and worship facilities, developing long-term relationships with clients across the United States. The firm also partners with design associates such as RMK Design Associates for national custom furniture projects.

The company emphasizes a single-point-of-contact approach, with the same craftsmen overseeing fabrication through installation. It cites competitive pricing, quality workmanship, and professional customer service as core values, backed by decades of industry experience.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Woodworking", "Laminating", "Finishing", "Packaging and delivery", "Installation", "Project consulting", "Floor plan-based design and quoting", "NCIDQ-accredited interior design"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Educational", "Financial", "Restaurant", "Worship facilities"], "materials": ["Wood", "Laminates"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same craftsmen handle fabrication, delivery, and installation", "Woman- and veteran-owned", "NCIDQ-accredited designers on staff", "Nationwide installation capability", "Over 40 years of furniture industry experience"], "facts_used": ["Fort Wayne, Indiana headquarters -> db", "Woman- and veteran-owned -> /", "Nicole Kenefic, Purdue graduate 2003, with company since 2003 -> db", "Brian and Nicole acquired RMK Design Associates July 2018 -> db", "Over 40 years in furniture business -> /", "Custom furniture design, woodworking, laminating, finishing -> /", "Same craftsmen build, package, deliver, install -> /", "Team includes furniture artisans, NCIDQ-accredited designers, installation specialists -> /", "Nationwide installation travel -> /", "Industries: healthcare, educational, financial, restaurant, worship -> db", "Partnership with RMK Design Associates for national projects -> db", "Competitive pricing, quality workmanship, professional customer service -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design custom furniture tailored to your exact needs, specifications, and vision. From there, our skilled craftsmen hand-build each piece using premium-quality materials and exceptional attention to detail.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned", "Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kda-furniture-interiors' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='KFK Seasonings operates from Portland, Oregon. The company was founded with a vision to provide first-class seasonings and blending services to institutions and processors nationwide. It is organized as a limited liability company, and its senior executive team brings over 125 years of combined experience in seasonings, manufacturing, and distribution.

The company produces custom spice blends, flavoring systems, breading mixes, drink mixes, extracts, and colors. Its blending capabilities range from 300-pound batches to full truckloads, with portion packaging from one-pound bags to super sacks. An on-site R&D and quality-control laboratory supports formulation and technical services, staffed by in-house food technologists.

KFK serves food processors, institutional kitchens, and food-service distributors across the United States. Customers include manufacturers seeking private-label seasonings, as well as operators needing custom blends for specific applications.

The company emphasizes rigorous testing on every shipment and maintains full-service laboratory facilities at its headquarters to ensure purity and freshness. It traces its approach to the traditions of the historic spice trade, aiming to build long-term partnerships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom spice blending", "Flavoring system development", "Food service supply", "Private label manufacturing", "Institutional packaging", "Nutritional labeling", "Product development", "Research and development", "Quality control testing", "Laboratory analysis", "Portion packaging (1 lb to super sacks)", "Formulation services", "Technical support", "Spice and herb blending", "Dehydrated vegetable processing", "Breading mix production", "Drink mix production", "Extract and color blending"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Food service", "Institutional food service"], "materials": ["Spices", "Herbs", "Dehydrated vegetables", "Breading mixes", "Drink mixes", "Extracts", "Colors"], "equipment": [], "volume": "300 lb to truckload quantities; portion packs from 1 lb to super sacks", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["State-of-the-art blending capabilities with capacities from 300 lb to truckload quantities", "Portion pack sizing from 1 pound to super sacks", "In-house food technologists providing formulation and technical services", "Full-service R&D/QC laboratory on site at Portland headquarters", "Rigorous testing performed on every shipment"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Portland, Oregon -> db", "Founded with vision to provide first-class seasonings and blending services -> /about", "Senior executive group brings over 125 years combined experience -> /about", "Blending capacities from 300 lb to truckload quantities -> /about", "Portion pack sizing from 1 pound to super sacks -> /about", "In-house food technologists provide formulation and technical services -> /about", "Full-service R&D/QC laboratory on site -> /about", "Rigorous testing on every shipment -> /about", "Products include custom spice blends, flavoring systems, breading mixes, drink mixes, extracts, colors -> /", "Serves food processors, institutions, food service -> /about", "Company is KFK Seasonings, LLC -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "KFK features state of the art blending capabilities, with capacities ranging from 300 lb. to truckload quantities.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/1321099/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kfk-seasonings' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='KSport USA was founded in 2003 in Mesa, Arizona. The company specializes in performance suspension systems for competitive driving, offering a range of coilover and air suspension products.

The company designs and manufactures coilover systems, air suspension components, and replacement parts for a variety of vehicle platforms. Its product lineup includes the Slide Kontrol coilover series, Airtech air suspension components, and associated hardware kits. A noted feature is a slim top-plate design with a hardened rubber coating intended to increase durability and reduce noise. The company also provides a replacement-part identification service, allowing customers to submit photos for quick part matching.

KSport USA serves the automotive aftermarket and motorsports segments, with particular emphasis on drift competition. Its components are built to withstand the high loads and abuse encountered on drift circuits, and the company also supplies replacement parts for existing installations. The firm works with aerospace-grade aluminum for certain components, indicating a focus on high-strength materials.

The business was established to provide suspension products that meet the demands of competitive drivers, focusing on strength and reliability under extreme conditions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Coilover design and manufacturing", "Air suspension component manufacturing", "Replacement parts sourcing and identification", "Custom top-plate fabrication with hardened rubber coating"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Motorsports (drift)", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["Aluminum (aerospace quality)", "Hardened rubber"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Designed for competitive-level performance on drift circuits", "Slim top-plate design with hardened rubber coating for durability and quietness", "Replacement-part identification via photo submission", "Use of aerospace-quality aluminum in components"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2003 -> db", "Headquartered in Mesa, Arizona -> db", "Produces Slide Kontrol coilovers and Airtech air suspension components -> db", "Offers replacement parts and identification service -> db", "Uses aerospace-quality aluminum and hardened rubber coating -> db", "Targets drift circuit competition -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Ksport Slide Kontrol Coilovers were designed to perform at a competitive level and withstand the abuse of the drift circuit", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ksport-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kaempf & Harris Sheet Metal operates from Frederick, Maryland, where it was founded in 1941 as part of the R.W. Warner family of companies. The business reached its third generation of family ownership in 1998 when Matt Warner became CEO, continuing a lineage that traces back to 1937 under the Warner name. Today it functions as a division alongside Warner Service, Warner Construction, and Warner Mechanical.

The shop focuses on precision sheet metal fabrication for commercial, industrial, and institutional projects. Core processes include CNC laser cutting, press brake forming, turret punching, welding, riveting, and fastening, with finishing options such as painting, powder coating, and galvanizing. The company reports fabricating more than 500 tons of metal annually—aluminum, steel, copper, stainless steel, galvanized steel, and black iron—and cites a single project, Frederick’s Rose Hill Cancer Center, that required over 75,000 pounds of sheet metal. Design-build services integrate design and construction under a single point of contact, and crews also handle on-site installation of the fabricated components.

Customers span mechanical contractors, general contractors, corporations, and institutions across healthcare, sports and entertainment, commercial construction, industrial manufacturing, and infrastructure. Notable references include the Rose Hill Cancer Center and the Hagerstown Multi-Use Sports Event Center, a $59.5 million project authorized by the Maryland Stadium Authority in 2021.

Kaempf & Harris emphasizes a design-build model that streamlines delivery and reduces rework, backed by American Institute of Steel Construction (AISC) fabricator certification and active membership in the Sheet Metal and Air Conditioning Contractors’ National Association (SMACNA). A dedicated in-house safety program, including OSHA 10/30 and specialized trade training, supports its focus on mission-critical environments where uptime and coordination are essential.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC certified fabricator','SMACNA member']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication", "Design-build services", "Metal fabrication (structural components)", "Sheet metal installation", "CNC laser cutting", "Press brake forming", "Turret punching", "Welding", "Riveting", "Fastening", "Painting", "Powder coating", "Galvanizing", "Custom ductwork fabrication", "Pipe supports fabrication", "Equipment bases fabrication", "Custom brackets and frames"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Industrial manufacturing", "Infrastructure", "Healthcare", "Sports and entertainment", "Institutional", "Mechanical contracting", "General contracting"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Copper", "Stainless steel", "Galvanized steel", "Black iron steel"], "equipment": ["CNC lasers", "Press brakes", "Turret punches"], "volume": "500+ tons annually; projects of any scale", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design-build integration of design and construction under single point of contact", "AISC certified fabricator", "SMACNA member", "500+ tons annual fabrication capacity across multiple metal types", "In-house safety training program with OSHA 10/30 and trade-specific certifications", "Mission-critical project experience in healthcare and sports venues"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Frederick, Maryland -> db", "Founded 1941 -> /services", "Third-generation family ownership, Matt Warner CEO 1998 -> /about-us", "Part of R.W. Warner family of companies (Warner Service, Warner Construction, Warner Mechanical) -> /about-us", "Fabricates 500+ tons metal annually -> /about-us", "Materials: aluminum, steel, copper, stainless steel, galvanized steel, black iron steel -> /about-us, /", "Equipment: CNC lasers, press brakes, turret punches -> /, /services", "Processes: cutting, bending, shaping, welding, riveting, fastening -> /, /services", "Finishing: painting, powder coating, galvanizing -> /, /services", "Design-build services with single point of contact -> /, /services", "Sheet metal installation services -> /, /services", "Rose Hill Cancer Center project: 75,000+ lbs sheet metal -> /, /services", "Hagerstown Multi-Use Sports Event Center project (2021, $59.5M) -> /, /about-us", "Industries: commercial, industrial, institutional, construction, industrial manufacturing, infrastructure, healthcare, sports -> /services, /", "Customer types: mechanical companies, general contractors, corporations, institutions -> /about-us", "AISC certified fabricator -> /services", "SMACNA member -> /services", "In-house safety program with OSHA 10/30, fall protection, MEWP, scaffolding, confined space, CPR, etc. -> /", "Mission-critical project specialization -> /", "Quality, Loyalty, Integrity values -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our services at Kaempf & Harris focus on precision sheet metal fabrication for commercial and industrial applications.", "founded_year": "1941", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kaempf-harris-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1926 in Honolulu, Hawaii, Kaimuki Dry Goods has operated as a fabric and sewing supply retailer for nearly a century.

The store carries thousands of items across hundreds of fabric styles, including the state''s largest selection of Kona cotton solids and exclusive Asian fabrics. It also stocks notions such as buttons and ribbons, patterns from collections like New Looks, Victoria Jones, and Apapane Designs, and a range of sewing machines for every skill level. In addition to retail, the company provides sewing machine repair services—both general and specialized for embroidery and computerized machines—with complimentary estimates performed by certified technicians. Sewing classes, from beginner basics to specialty techniques, round out the offerings.

The company emphasizes its long-standing presence since 1926, a curated selection of unique fabrics, and a full-service model that combines retail, repair, and education. Free estimates on machine repairs and knowledgeable, friendly staff are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sewing machine repair (general)", "Sewing machine repair (specialized for embroidery and computerized machines)", "Sewing classes (basic)", "Sewing classes (specialty)", "Retail of fabrics, notions, patterns, and sewing machines"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Kona cotton solids", "Asian fabrics", "Various fabric prints and solids"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Operating continuously since 1926", "State''s largest selection of Kona cotton solids and exclusive Asian fabrics", "Complete sewing center: fabrics, notions, patterns, machines, repairs, and classes", "Free estimates on sewing machine repairs", "Certified technicians for general and specialized sewing machine repairs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1926 -> db", "Headquarters Honolulu, Hawaii -> db", "Offers fabrics, notions, patterns, sewing machines -> /", "Provides sewing machine repair services with free estimates -> /", "Offers sewing classes (basic and specialty) -> /", "Certified technicians for repairs -> /", "Operating since 1926 -> /", "Largest selection of Kona cotton solids in state -> /", "Exclusive Asian fabrics -> /"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "At Kaimuki Dry Goods, we take pride in our extensive product range, offering a vast selection of thousands of items.", "founded_year": "1926", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kaimuki-dry-goods-ltd' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kamuela Hardwoods operates from Waimea, Hawaii, where co-owners Alex Woodbury and Joshua Greenspan—an ISA‑certified arborist—founded the company as a partnership between an arborist and a woodworker. The business began with a mission to salvage urban and felled trees that would otherwise be burned, chipped, or landfilled, turning that material into usable lumber.

The sawmill processes over 30 Hawaiian and exotic hardwood species—including koa, monkeypod, mango, Norfolk pine, lychee, eucalyptus, and ohia—into live‑edge slabs, kiln‑dried lumber, and bowl blanks. A kiln‑drying step ensures dimensional stability for fine woodworking and instrument making. The operation runs on locally produced bio‑diesel and follows a zero‑waste model: offcuts become utility lumber or garden materials, while sawdust and chips are converted to mulch and soil amendments.

Customers include furniture makers, woodworkers, instrument builders, artisans, and builders across Hawaii, the continental U.S., and internationally. The company ships slabs and lumber for cabinetry, countertops, flooring, and custom projects, with an online inventory that allows buyers to select specific pieces.

Woodbury and Greenspan frame the venture as a deliberate alternative to unnecessary tree removal: "We are trying to do something different, we don''t want to unnecessarily remove a tree for any reason," Woodbury says. Greenspan adds, "It''s unfortunate when a tree has to come down, but in a sense, we''re giving it a new life." That ethos drives the salvage‑first approach and the minimal‑waste processing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISA Certified Arborist']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Urban timber salvage", "Sawmilling", "Kiln drying", "Live-edge slab milling", "Bowl blank production", "Custom milling", "Wood waste recycling", "Bio-diesel powered operations"], "industries": ["Furniture making", "Woodworking", "Musical instrument manufacturing", "Artisan crafts", "Construction", "Cabinetry", "Flooring"], "materials": ["Koa (Acacia Koa)", "Monkeypod (Monkey Pod)", "Mango", "Norfolk Pine", "Lychee", "Eucalyptus Robusta", "Eucalyptus Saligna", "Lehua Ohia", "Toon", "Podocarpus", "Silk Oak", "Blue Gum", "Red Gum", "Australian Blackwood", "Citrus Wood", "Keawe"], "equipment": ["Sawmill", "Kiln"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Urban timber salvage diverting trees from landfill or burn piles", "Zero\u2011waste processing: all byproducts become utility lumber, mulch, or soil amendments", "Kiln\u2011dried lumber for stability in fine woodworking and instruments", "Over 30 Hawaiian and exotic hardwood species available", "Equipment powered by locally produced bio\u2011diesel"], "facts_used": ["Located in Waimea, Hawaii -> db", "Co-owned by Alex Woodbury and Joshua Greenspan -> /about-us", "Formed by partnership between an arborist and a woodworker -> /about-us", "Specializes in reclaimed Hawaiian timber, live-edge slabs, premium hardwood lumber -> /", "Over 30 Hawaiian and exotic hardwood species -> /", "Products include live-edge slabs, kiln-dried lumber, bowl blanks -> /", "Kiln-drying process ensures stability -> /", "Zero-waste operation: byproducts repurposed into utility lumber, mulch, garden materials -> /", "Equipment operated on locally produced bio-diesel -> /about-us", "Ships across Hawaii, U.S., internationally -> /", "Serves furniture makers, woodworkers, instrument builders, artisans, builders -> /", "ISA Certified Arborist co-owner Joshua Greenspan -> /about-us", "Sustainability focus: urban timber salvage -> /about-us", "Team includes Austin Iban, Jessica Salerno-Woodbury, Elton Alameda, Chris Eblacas, Madison Bartlett, Jimmy Wray -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kamuela Hardwoods is an urban timber salvage company", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kamuela-hardwoods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kanson Electronics Inc. operates from a 30,000-square-foot manufacturing and technical center in Hohenwald, Tennessee. The company traces its roots to 1963 when it began producing ISSC timers, sensors, and counters in the United States. The business is veteran-owned; it was also woman-owned from 1979 until 2013.

The firm manufactures its own line of industrial timers and sensors, offering variable timing ranges, encapsulated circuitry, and powder-coated enclosures. In addition to its proprietary products, Kanson provides contract manufacturing for electrical and electro-mechanical subassemblies and complete systems. Capabilities include screen printing, powder coating, and 100 percent testing and quality cycling of every unit.

Kanson serves customers ranging from small businesses to Fortune 200 companies across industrial and electronic markets. Its timers and sensors are used in applications requiring accurate timing control and isolation between voltages, while its contract assembly services address custom subassembly and system-level needs.

