 electrical and electro-mechanical subassembly and systems.", "founded_year": "1963", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned", "Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kanson-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kase Custom was founded in 2014 in Mesa, Arizona. The company began with a single table and a belief that craftsmanship and connection matter.

The shop produces made-to-order reclaimed wood furniture, including bar-height, counter-height, and dining-height tables, as well as coffee tables. Each piece is handcrafted in their Arizona facility using a process that starts with a complimentary design consultation, followed by hand fabrication and finishing. The company reports over 5,500 orders delivered and a current build time of four to six weeks.

Kase Custom serves both commercial and residential customers. In the hospitality sector, its tables are used by international hotel brands and local coffee shops. For residential clients, the furniture is built for busy family kitchens and everyday gathering spaces.

The company differentiates itself through a "slow furniture" philosophy—building pieces to last decades rather than seasons. It emphasizes custom dimensions to fit any space, a complimentary design service, and its status as a Certified B Corporation, reflecting a commitment to social and environmental performance.', certifications=ARRAY['Certified B Corporation']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted wood fabrication", "Reclaimed wood sourcing", "Finish application", "Complimentary design consultation", "Made-to-order manufacturing"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Reclaimed wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "4-6 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom dimensions for every piece", "Complimentary design consultation", "Handcrafted in Arizona from reclaimed wood", "Certified B Corporation", "4-6 week build time"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 -> db", "Headquarters Mesa, Arizona -> db", "Certified B Corporation -> /", "5,500+ orders delivered -> /", "Current build time 4-6 weeks -> /", "Serves hospitality (international hotel brands, local coffee shops) -> /", "Serves residential (family kitchens, gathering spaces) -> /", "Complimentary design service -> /", "Handcrafted reclaimed wood furniture -> /", "Started with one table -> /", "Custom dimensions (length, height, finish) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Built by hand in Arizona since 2014", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kase-custom-custom-wood-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kayem Foods traces its roots to 1909 when Kazimierz Monkiewicz opened a modest butcher shop in Chelsea, Massachusetts. Now in its fifth generation of family ownership, the company remains headquartered in Chelsea and operates as the largest prepared-meat producer in New England.

The facility turns out more than 200 products across ten brands, covering frankfurters, sausages, bacon, slow-cooked meats, deli selections, and breakfast links and patties.

Customers range from home cooks and grill enthusiasts to chefs, restaurants, retailers, and major sports venues such as ballparks and stadiums across the United States. The portfolio is built for both retail shelves and foodservice channels.

The business emphasizes community engagement, sustainability targets — including a 20 percent reduction goal for water, CO2, and cardboard use — and animal-welfare commitments through membership in the Meat Institute and the Protein Pact.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Meat processing", "Sausage manufacturing", "Bacon curing and smoking", "Slow-cooked meat preparation", "Deli meat slicing and packaging", "Breakfast sausage production"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Meat processing", "Foodservice", "Retail", "Stadium and venue catering"], "materials": ["Pork", "Beef", "Chicken"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest prepared meat company in New England", "Over 200 products across 10 brands", "5th generation family-owned and operated", "Member of Meat Institute and Protein Pact", "Zero-sort recycling implemented in plants"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1909 by Kazimierz Monkiewicz -> /about", "5th generation family-owned and operated -> /about", "Headquartered in Chelsea, MA -> /about", "Largest prepared meat company in New England -> /about", "Over 200 products across 10 brands -> /about", "Over 200 employees -> /about", "Manufactures in Chelsea, MA -> /", "Products: frankfurters, sausages, bacon, slow-cooked meats, deli, breakfast -> /", "Serves home cooks, chefs, restaurants, stadiums, retailers -> /", "Member of Meat Institute and Protein Pact -> /about", "Sustainability goals: reduce water, CO2, cardboard by 20% -> /about", "Zero-sort recycling in plants -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We proudly manufacture our products in Chelsea, MA.", "founded_year": "1909", "employee_count": "over 200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kayem-foods-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kelly Ryan Equipment Company was founded in 1945 in Blair, Nebraska, by Kelly Ryan. The company began by building portable farm elevators from whatever materials were available, including scrap, to meet post-war farmer demand.

Today the company operates two primary lines: farm equipment manufacturing and steel fabrication under the KRECO name. The farm line includes grain baggers, Feed-R-Wagon feeders for livestock, and manure spreaders ranging from 4 to 7 feet.

The farm equipment serves grain and livestock producers across the agriculture market, with baggers that help farmers harvest faster and manage weather risk, and feed wagons designed for cattle, horses, sheep, and goats.

