UPDATE companies SET description='Kester Foods operates from Eugene, Oregon, with a production facility in southern Oregon. The company, organized as a limited liability company, produces two branded lines: Vegan Burger and Northwest Fork. No founding year or founder names are disclosed in public materials.

The company manufactures dry‑mix vegan burgers and emergency food kits. Its Vegan Burger blend combines gluten‑free oats, black and pinto beans, dehydrated vegetables, and organic brown rice; preparation requires only hot water and a five‑minute rest before forming and grilling patties. The Northwest Fork line targets emergency preparedness with similar clean‑label ingredients. Both lines are produced in a facility certified vegan and kosher. Specific facility size, headcount, or annual volume are not published.

Kester Foods serves the plant‑based food market and the emergency‑preparedness sector.

The company emphasizes that its mixes contain no artificial ingredients, preservatives, GMOs, gluten, or soy, positioning them as allergy‑friendly and simple to prepare. The Northwest Fork brand was created to provide emergency rations without compromising dietary restrictions.', certifications=ARRAY['Vegan certified','Kosher certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Dry mix blending", "Vegan burger mix production", "Emergency food kit assembly", "Gluten-free production", "Allergen-controlled manufacturing", "Kosher certified production", "Vegan certified production"], "industries": ["Plant-based food manufacturing", "Emergency preparedness food", "Allergy-friendly food", "Vegan food products"], "materials": ["Gluten free oats", "Black beans", "Pinto beans", "Dehydrated vegetables", "Organic brown rice"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vegan and kosher certified production facility", "Free from artificial ingredients, preservatives, GMOs, gluten, and soy", "Allergy\u2011friendly formulations", "Simple preparation: just add hot water", "Emergency food line with clean\u2011label ingredients"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Eugene, Oregon -> db", "Produces Vegan Burger and Northwest Fork brands -> /", "Vegan and kosher certified facility in southern Oregon -> /", "Ingredients: gluten free oats, black and pinto beans, dehydrated vegetables, organic brown rice -> /", "Company organized as Kester Foods, LLC -> /", "Phone and hours listed -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Makers of Northwest Fork and Vegan Burger brands", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kester-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Key Packaging Co operates from Sarasota, Florida, specializing in custom thin-gauge thermoformed plastic packaging. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The firm provides end-to-end thermoforming services, including design and prototyping, in-house mold and tool building, thermoforming production, supply chain management, and quality assurance. Its capabilities cover a range of industries requiring protective and shipping trays, as well as retail and medical packaging.

Key Packaging serves medical device, pharmaceutical, automotive, cosmetic, retail, electronics, and food packaging markets. Customers include manufacturers needing protective trays for automotive and industrial components, as well as medical and pharmaceutical packaging that meets stringent quality requirements.

