UPDATE companies SET description='Key Woodworking, Inc. operates from Springfield, Virginia, in the Washington, D.C. metro area. The company was founded in 1992 by a first-generation immigrant who began as a one-man woodworking shop. Through decades of sustained effort, the business has grown into a small but capable firm serving the commercial construction market.

The shop specializes in custom-fabricated premium architectural woodwork, providing engineering services to align fabrication with design intent and managing material procurement from global sources including Europe, Africa, and Asia. Its craftsmen combine extensive experience with modern equipment to execute projects that have reached single-contract values exceeding $2 million, often on compressed schedules.

Key Woodworking focuses on upscale high-rise multi-residential buildings and Class A office towers, along with restaurants and public institutions throughout the DMV region. Past work includes amenity spaces, lobbies, and lounges for prominent developments in the Washington, D.C. area.

The company emphasizes a value set described as honest, hard-working, and innovative, backed by operational practices such as finely tuned scheduling, open communication, and a policy of taking full ownership of each project. These principles, the firm says, differentiate it from competitors and have sustained client relationships for over 30 years.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom architectural woodworking", "Engineering services for design intent verification", "Global material procurement and sourcing", "Project scheduling and management", "Design-to-fabrication coordination"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "High-rise multi-residential buildings", "Class A office buildings", "Restaurants", "Public institutions"], "materials": ["Wood (globally sourced)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Worldwide wood sourcing from Europe, Africa, and Asia", "Custom architectural woodworking for high-rise multi-residential and Class A office projects", "Engineering services to ensure design intent is met", "Proven ability to deliver contracts over $2 million on tight deadlines", "Finely tuned scheduling and open communication centered on integrity"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Springfield, Virginia -> db", "Founder: first-generation immigrant started one-man shop -> /about", "Custom architectural woodworking for commercial projects -> /, /services", "Specialty in upscale high-rise multi-residential and Class A office buildings -> /, /services", "Engineering services to ensure design intent -> /, /services", "Worldwide material sourcing (Europe, Africa, Asia) -> /about", "Single contracts of $2M+ with tight deadlines -> /about", "30+ years experience -> /about", "Small business -> /about", "Values: honest, hard working, innovative -> /about", "Differentiators: pride in dedication, tuned scheduling, open communication, ownership of project, innovative solutions -> /services", "Industries served: commercial, high-rise multi-residential, Class A office, restaurants, public institutions -> /about", "Project types: amenity spaces, lobbies, lounges -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We service the commercial community with Custom fabricated premium architectural woodwork", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='key-woodworking-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Keyser Manufacturing operates from Coopersville, Michigan, where it produces race car components and provides contract fabrication services for a range of industries. The company describes itself as one of the largest manufacturers of race car parts in the United States, while also building custom parts for clients in automotive, tool and die, chemical, transportation, and other sectors.

Its in-house capabilities span CNC machining (lathes and mills), laser cutting with a Mitsubishi 2D LP Plus II 3,500-watt CO2 laser, waterjet cutting up to six inches thick, turret punching on a Strippit 1000/20 press, rolling and forming, and welding (MIG, TIG, and robotic cells). The shop also runs powder coating, anodizing, 3D printing for rapid prototypes, and a dedicated shock absorber development program. The company notes it can handle volumes from a single prototype to production runs of thousands, and its online catalog lists over 12,000 stocked products.

The firm''s OMI ATV Products line targets off-road enthusiasts with shocks, cooling components, body parts, and suspension pieces.

Keyser Manufacturing emphasizes its willingness to quote jobs that other shops decline, along with quick turnaround times and in-house engineering support. Its waterjet process avoids heat-affected zones, and robotic welding cells improve consistency on larger orders.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining (lathes, mills)", "Laser cutting (CO2, up to 60\" x 120\")", "Waterjet cutting (dynamic, up to 6\" thick)", "Turret punching (CNC, 20-station)", "Rolling and forming", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Robotic welding", "Powder coating", "Anodizing", "3D printing (rapid prototyping)", "Shock absorber development", "Engineering design", "Assembly"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Tool and die", "Chemical", "Transportation", "Craft production", "Industrial equipment", "Shipping", "Government", "Racing", "Powersports/ATV"], "materials": ["Steel (high carbon)", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Rubber", "Foam", "Composites", "Stone", "Ceramic", "Tile", "Paper", "Metal alloys"], "equipment": ["Mitsubishi 2D LP Plus II 3500 watt CO2 Laser", "Strippit 1000/20 CNC Turret Punch Press", "CNC Lathes", "CNC Mills", "Manual machining equipment", "Robotic welding cells (minimum 10 MIG cells)", "3D printer", "Waterjet cutting system"], "volume": "Prototype to thousands", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.00039 in (laser cutting repeatable accuracy)", "built_on": ["In-house CNC machining for quick turnaround on prototypes and production runs", "Willingness to quote jobs other shops decline", "Waterjet cutting with no heat-affected zone", "Robotic welding cells for consistency on high-volume orders", "3D printing delivers working prototypes in hours"], "facts_used": ["Location: Coopersville, Michigan -> db", "Self-described as one of the largest manufacturers of race car parts in the US -> /services", "In-house capabilities: CNC machining, laser cutting, waterjet, turret punching, rolling/forming, welding, powder coating, anodizing, 3D printing