UPDATE companies SET description='Keystone Electrical Manufacturing Company has operated from Des Moines, Iowa since 1964. The company designs and builds power protection and control equipment for the electrical generation, transmission, and distribution sectors.

Its vertically integrated facility handles sheet metal fabrication, assembly, wiring, and testing in-house. The product line includes protection and control panels (line, distribution, transformer, bus differential, annunciator, feeder, metering, communication, SCADA/RTU), substation control centers ranging from 20-by-14-foot to 60-by-30-foot buildings, power distribution centers from 5 kV to 35 kV, medium voltage switchgear up to 38 kV, and low voltage control panels for OEMs. Engineering support services cover detailed bills of material, point-to-point wiring diagrams, AC/DC schematics, and as-built documentation.

Customers include electric utilities, utility-scale wind turbine and transformer manufacturers, voltage regulation system builders, industrial machinery OEMs, and renewable energy integrators. Keystone also works with overseas OEMs serving the U.S. market to meet NEC and UL 508A requirements.

The company cites its single-point project management, documented quality assurance program with in-process and final testing using a Doble F6150e test set, Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot, and custom breaker simulator, and the option for customer facility inspections as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering support services", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Electrical assembly and wiring", "Protection & control panel manufacturing", "Substation control center assembly", "Power distribution center assembly (5\u201335 kV)", "Medium voltage switchgear assembly (up to 38 kV)", "Low voltage control panel manufacturing", "Motor control panel manufacturing", "PLC control panel manufacturing", "VFD and reduced voltage starter panels", "RTU and SCADA cabinet manufacturing", "Junction box fabrication", "Custom enclosure fabrication", "Off-the-shelf enclosure supply", "DC battery system installation", "Termination cabinet installation", "HVAC, lighting, security, safety system installation", "Inter-panel wiring and cabling", "Point-to-point continuity testing", "Relay acceptance testing", "High voltage (Hi-Pot) testing", "Functional testing per IEEE/ANSI standards", "Three-phase current/potential injection testing"], "industries": ["Electrical generation", "Electrical transmission", "Electrical distribution", "Electric utilities", "Utility-scale wind turbine manufacturing", "Utility-scale transformer manufacturing", "Utility-scale breaker manufacturing", "Voltage regulation systems", "Industrial machinery", "Renewable energy generation systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Doble F6150e test set", "Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot", "Custom breaker simulator"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated facility (sheet metal, assembly, wiring, testing)", "Single-point project management for each contract", "Detailed as-built construction and maintenance documentation", "Rigorous in-process and final testing with Doble F6150e, Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot, custom breaker simulator", "Customer facility visits welcomed for inspections and testing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1964 -> /", "Headquarters Des Moines, Iowa -> db", "Vertically integrated facility with sheet metal fabrication, assembly, wiring, testing -> /", "Protection & control panels (line, distribution, transformer, bus differential, annunciator, feeder, metering, communication, SCADA/RTU) -> /", "Substation control centers 20x14 ft to 60x30 ft -> /", "Power distribution centers 5 kV to 35 kV -> /", "Medium voltage switchgear up to 38 kV -> /", "Low voltage control panels for OEMs (motor control, PLC, VFD, RTU/SCADA) -> /", "Industries: utilities, wind turbine, transformer, breaker, voltage regulation, industrial machinery, renewable energy -> /", "Engineering support: BOM, wiring diagrams, schematics, as-built docs -> /", "Single-point project management -> /", "Testing equipment: Doble F6150e, Peschel 100 kV Hi-Pot, custom breaker simulator -> /", "Testing per IEEE/ANSI standards, three-phase injection, phase angle meter, DC scheme verification -> /", "Customer facility visits for inspection -> /", "Works with overseas OEMs for NEC/UL 508A compliance -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture products for the electrical generation, transmission, and distribution markets. ... With a vertically integrated facility that includes sheet metal fabrication, assembly, wiring, and testing, we custom-manufacture systems to meet even the most exacting standards.", "founded_year": "1964", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='keystone-electrical-manufacturing-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ki USA Corporation has operated from Berea, Kentucky since 1989 as a subsidiary of American Industrial Acquisition Corporation. The company began as a manufacturer of automotive engine, body, and suspension components.

The firm specializes in precision metal stamping, robotic welding, and electro-coat finishing, delivering products such as engine mounts, brake boosters, and oil pans. Its 250,000-square-foot Kentucky facility on 54 acres employs about 160 associates, while a subsidiary in Irapuato, Mexico adds 45 employees and 3,288 square meters of production space. The vertically integrated platform combines stamping, welding, and e-coat under one roof, supported by programmable robotic welding systems and automated material handling.

Ki USA primarily serves the automotive industry, supplying Honda, Mazda, and Ford for internal combustion, hybrid, and electric vehicle platforms. It is expanding into power generation and home appliance sectors, leveraging its high-volume automotive and industrial production capabilities.

The company emphasizes trust, transparency, and continuous improvement, with an in-house e-coat line that ensures faster turnaround and strict quality control. Community involvement includes support for Relay For Life and Soles4Souls.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16969:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision metal stamping", "Robotic welding", "Welded assemblies", "Electro-coat (E-Coat) finishing", "Automated material handling"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Power Generation", "Home appliances", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Steel"], "equipment": ["Programmable robotic welding systems", "Automated material handling equipment", "Electro-coat (E-Coat) line"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully integrated manufacturing platform combining stamping, robotic welding, and e-coat under one roof", "Vertically integrated approach for cost-competitive, high-quality solutions", "Extensive automation including programmable robotic welding systems and automated material handling", "Localized support via Mexico subsidiary for customers throughout Mexico", "In-house electro-coat line ensuring faster turnaround and strict quality control"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 in Berea, Kentucky -> /about", "Subsidiary of American Industrial Acquisition Corporation -> /about", "250,000 sq ft facility on 54 acres, 160 US employees -> /about", "Mexico subsidiary in Irapuato, 45 employees, started June 2015 -> /about", "Processes: precision metal stamping, robotic welding, electro-coat finishing -> /about and /", "Products: engine mounts, brake boosters, engine oil pans -> /about", "Customers: Honda, Mazda, Ford -> db (description)", "Industries: automotive, power generation, home appliances -> /", "Certification: IATF 16969:2016 -> /about", "Equipment: programmable robotic welding systems, automated material handling -> /about", "Employees 200+ total -> /", "Community involvement: Relay For Life, Soles4Souls -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Since 1989, KI (USA) has been a leading manufacturer of automotive engine, body, and suspension components in Berea, Kentucky.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "200+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ki-usa-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kibberia Foods operates commercial kitchens in Danbury, Connecticut and Lafayette, Louisiana. The company was founded by Carole Iskandar and her husband Sam, who began as restaurant owners in Danbury over a decade ago serving authentic Mediterranean cuisine. The business is family owned and operated. In 2021, they expanded to Lafayette to serve southeastern retailers.

The company produces more than 350 recipes, including an established line of 250-plus SKUs of all-natural, restaurant-quality prepared foods. Its capabilities include recipe research and development, rapid scale-up from concept to mass production within a week, and large-scale production with same-day ingredient processing. Facilities are SQF and HACCP certified, USDA inspected, and FSMA-ready.

Kibberia Foods supplies large retailers and supermarkets, offering products in individual, family-size, and food-service packaging. The company collaborates with retail partners to develop private-label lines and adjusts formulations for target price points, seasonal demand, and demographic preferences.

Founder Carole Iskandar’s Mediterranean heritage and commitment to food safety drive the mission to deliver fresh, healthy, nutritious food at cost-effective prices. The company emphasizes a boutique approach to recipe creation, donates surplus food to local charities, and maintains annual performance audits to ensure quality.', certifications=ARRAY['HACCP','SQF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Recipe development and research", "New product development (concept to mass production in 1 week)", "Large-scale food production", "Co-packing and private label manufacturing", "Food packaging (individual, family size, food service)", "HACCP plan implementation", "SQF compliance", "USDA inspected facility", "Same-day ingredient processing", "Fresh-to-order production", "Flexible formulation for price, seasonality, demographics", "Trend analysis and menu consulting"], "industries": ["Food retail", "Supermarkets", "Food service", "Grocery retail"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "1 week for new product development to mass production", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family owned and operated commercial kitchens in Connecticut and Louisiana", "SQF and HACCP certified, USDA inspected, FSMA-ready facilities", "Over 350 recipes developed by in-house chefs", "New product development to mass production in one week", "Same-day ingredient receipt and production for maximum freshness"], "facts_used": ["Family owned and operated commercial kitchen -> /", "Founder Carole Iskandar and husband Sam -> /", "Started as restaurant owners in Danbury, CT over 10 years ago -> /", "Expanded to Lafayette, LA in 2021 -> /", "Two kitchens in Danbury, CT and Lafayette, LA -> /", "Over 350 recipes cooked by in-house chefs -> /", "Established line of 250+ SKUs -> /", "SQF and HACCP certified -> /", "USDA on site -> /", "FSMA-ready facility -> /", "Rapid response new product development to mass production in a week -> /", "All ingredients received and produced same day 