UPDATE companies SET description='Kindel Grand Rapids, based in Grand Rapids, Michigan, traces its roots to 1886 when Albert F. Karges began making furniture in Evansville, Indiana. The modern entity formed when Kindel Furniture (founded 1901 by Charles J. Kindel) acquired Karges and Councill Furniture (founded 1973 by Fred and Hope Councill). The Fisher family has owned the business since 1964, maintaining a family-owned, 100% American-made operation.

The company produces made-to-order, handcrafted luxury furniture from its Grand Rapids facility. Offerings span dining, occasional, bedroom, and workspace collections, each built to customer specifications. The operation emphasizes domestic production, using traditional woodworking methods rather than offshore manufacturing.

Customers include residential clients seeking signature pieces and commercial offices requiring custom desks, tables, and credenzas. The Councill line has served workplace needs since 1973, while the Kindel and Karges brands address high-end home furnishings.

Kindel Grand Rapids differentiates itself through a commitment to domestic craftsmanship, preserving over 300 years of collective experience across its three heritage brands. The company states that every piece is made to precise customer specifications in its Michigan workshop, rejecting lower-cost offshore alternatives.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Made-to-order furniture manufacturing", "Handcrafted furniture production", "Custom furniture design"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Commercial office furniture"], "materials": ["Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% American-made furniture", "Handcrafted to precise customer specifications", "Made-to-order production", "Over 300 years of collective heritage across Kindel, Karges, and Councill", "Family-owned since 1964"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1886 (Karges) -> db", "Kindel founded 1901 by Charles J. Kindel -> /about", "Councill founded 1973 by Fred and Hope Councill -> /about", "Family-owned since 1964 by Fisher family -> /about", "Headquarters in Grand Rapids, Michigan -> /about", "Made-to-order, handcrafted luxury furniture -> / and /about", "Product categories: dining, occasional, bedroom, workspace -> /", "Office furniture since 1973 (Councill) -> /about", "100% American-made commitment -> /about", "Over 300 years collective experience -> /about", "Virtual 3D showroom tour -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Producing the world''s finest handcrafted, made-to-order pieces, we offer the best in American craftsmanship.", "founded_year": "1886", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kindel-furniture-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='King''s Wood Creation operates from Phoenix, Arizona, where it began over two decades ago as a one-man shop. The company has grown into a full-scale woodworking facility producing custom cabinets, doors, mantels, beams, furniture, and architectural millwork.

The shop runs CNC machinery alongside traditional woodworking equipment to fabricate kitchen and bath cabinetry, fireplace mantels, ceiling box beams, hand railings, and custom furniture. Services include design rendering, finishing, and carving, with the ability to source specialty timber on demand.

Clients range from residential homeowners to building professionals such as contractors, architects, and interior designers. The company has supplied millwork for new construction, remodels, and custom home projects throughout the Phoenix area.

King''s Wood Creation emphasizes material selection and in-house CNC capacity as differentiators, stating that it selects only the finest timber and can procure specialty woods as needed. The firm holds an Arizona Registrar of Contractors license (ROC #340054) and markets its products as proudly designed and produced in the USA.', certifications=ARRAY['ROC #340054']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining", "Custom cabinetry (kitchen and bath)", "Custom wood door manufacturing", "Fireplace mantel fabrication", "Ceiling box beam fabrication", "Custom furniture making", "Hand railing fabrication", "Wood finishing", "Wood carving", "Design and rendering services"], "industries": ["Building professionals", "Homeowners"], "materials": ["Timber", "Specialty woods"], "equipment": ["CNC (Computerized Numerical Control) machinery"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house CNC machining and experienced woodworking staff", "Specialty timber sourcing on demand", "Full-service woodworking facility from design to finish", "Arizona ROC licensed (ROC #340054)", "Custom architectural millwork for residential and commercial projects"], "facts_used": ["Company name: King''s Wood Creation -> db", "Headquarters: Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Founded over 20 years ago as a one-man shop -> /", "Products: custom wood doors, fireplace mantels, kitchen and bath cabinetry, ceiling box beams, furniture, hand railing, finishing, carvings -> /", "Processes: CNC machinery, woodworking -> /", "Materials: finest timber, specialty woods sourced on demand -> /", "Industries served: building professionals and homeowners -> /", "Certification: ROC #340054 -> /", "Facility: full woodworking facility -> /", "Tagline: Proudly designed & produced in the USA -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "KWC has developed into one of the premier manufacturers of fine wood products in the USA.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "