UPDATE companies SET description='Kit Clark Furniture operates from a studio in North Yarmouth, Maine, a rural community northwest of Portland. Clark relocated the operation to North Ferrisburgh, Vermont, in 2000, then moved again in the spring of 2016 to the current Maine location. A lifelong woodworker, Clark earned an associate degree in forestry from the University of New Hampshire and a bachelor’s in mine land reclamation from Montana State University, later apprenticing under his uncle, master carpenter Robert Clark, and studying Sam Maloof–style rocking chairs with chairwright Hal Taylor in 2007.

The studio produces bespoke, handcrafted furniture ranging from sculpted rocking chairs and dining sets to tables, beds, bedroom suites, bookcases, and custom accessories.

Testimonials reference clients in North Carolina, Singapore, and Massachusetts, and the company offers in-home design consultations for local projects.

Clark cites a lifetime guarantee—valid for as long as the original purchaser or their family owns the piece—as a core differentiator, along with the ability to recreate any gallery design in alternative wood combinations. The founder’s design philosophy draws on the fluid forms of nature, aiming to bring the peace of the outdoors into the home.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted furniture fabrication", "Sculpted rocking chair construction", "Dining table and chair set fabrication", "Bedroom furniture fabrication", "Bookcase construction", "Custom furniture accessories", "In-home design consultation", "Shipping and delivery (US, Canada, international)"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Wood (various species)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: North Yarmouth, Maine -> db", "Founder: Kit Clark -> /about", "Business opened in Bozeman, Montana (early 2000s) -> /about", "Relocated to North Ferrisburgh, Vermont in 2000 -> /about", "Moved to North Yarmouth, Maine in spring 2016 -> /about", "Education: Associate in Forestry (UNH), Bachelor in Mine Land Reclamation (Montana State) -> /about", "Apprenticed under uncle Robert Clark (master carpenter) -> /about", "Studied Sam Maloof-style rocking chairs with Hal Taylor in 2007 -> /about", "Lifetime guarantee on all pieces -> /about", "Ships anywhere in continental US and Canada -> /about", "Specializes in rocking chairs, chairs, dining sets, tables, beds, bookcases, custom accessories -> /services", "In-home consultation for local clients -> /about", "Custom wood combinations for any design -> /services", "Award-winning furniture maker claim -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "OFFERING A FULL LINE OF EXQUISITELY CRAFTED BESPOKE FURNITURE IN MAINE, SERVING PORTLAND AND CLIENTS NATIONWIDE", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_co