UPDATE companies SET description='Kulicke & Soffa Industries Inc. was founded in 1951 in Fort Washington, Pennsylvania. The company began as an innovator in semiconductor assembly technology and has since grown into a global supplier of equipment and solutions for the semiconductor packaging industry.

Its product portfolio also encompasses advanced dispensing solutions, aftermarket products, repair and refurbishment services, and spare parts supply. K&S operates globally, serving customers across multiple continents with a focus on advanced packaging technologies such as fluxless thermocompression bonding and co-packaged optics assembly.

K&S serves customers in the automotive, compute, industrial, memory, and communications markets.

Founded on a commitment to innovation, the company emphasizes aligning technology with opportunity to overcome dynamic process challenges. Recent recognitions include a SEMI Award for North America for breakthrough fluxless thermocompression bonding technology, underscoring its focus on pioneering capabilities that redefine semiconductor assembly and packaging.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire bonding", "Die bonding", "Thermocompression bonding", "Ultrasonic assembly", "Advanced packaging", "Fluxless bonding", "Co-packaged optics (CPO) assembly", "Aftermarket products and services", "Advanced dispensing solutions", "Equipment repair and refurbishment", "Spare parts supply"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Compute", "Industrial", "Memory", "Communications", "Semiconductor"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["ASTERION\u2122\u2011TW ultrasonic system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global leader in semiconductor assembly technology since 1951", "Breakthrough fluxless thermocompression bonding technology (SEMI Award recipient)", "Co-packaged optics (CPO) and advanced packaging leadership", "Ultrasonic assembly systems such as ASTERION\u2122\u2011TW for power electronics", "Comprehensive aftermarket support including repair, refurbishment, and spare parts"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1951 -> db", "Headquarters in Fort Washington, Pennsylvania -> db", "Global leader in semiconductor assembly technology -> db", "Serves automotive, compute, industrial, memory, communications markets -> db", "Offers aftermarket products and services, advanced dispensing solutions -> db", "Provides repair, refurbishment, and spare parts -> db", "ASTERION\u2122\u2011TW ultrasonic system launched -> page /", "SEMI Award for fluxless thermocompression bonding technology -> page /", "Co-packaged optics (CPO) and advanced packaging leadership -> page /", "75 years of legacy celebrated -> page /", "Website available in English, Chinese, Japanese -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Kulicke and Soffa is a global leader in semiconductor assembly technology", "founded_year": "1951", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Chinese", "Japanese"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='kulicke-soffa-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Kulite Semiconductor Products, Inc. was founded in 1959 by Dr. Anthony D. Kurtz in Leonia, New Jersey, just outside New York City. A physicist with degrees from MIT, Dr. Kurtz left Honeywell to establish a high‑technology company focused on pressure transduction. The business remains family‑founded and woman‑owned, now led by his widow, Nora Kurtz.

The company designs and manufactures pressure transducers, sensors, and switches for extreme environments. Its product line spans pressure ranges from 1 to 60,000 PSI, operating temperatures from ‑320 °F to 932 °F, and configurations including submersible, redundant, and hermetically sealed units. Kulite holds over 400 patents and operates a 200,000‑square‑foot, three‑building campus that houses research, manufacturing, and corporate offices, employing over 800 people.

Kulite serves aerospace and defense (commercial airliners such as the Boeing 747, military aircraft), automotive test and motorsport (Formula One, IndyCar), space exploration, marine, oil exploration, coal mining, and process‑control industries. Customers include OEMs, racing teams, and government agencies requiring high‑reliability pressure measurement.

The firm emphasizes that its differentiation lies in solving difficult pressure‑measurement problems: "whenever pressure or force needs to be measured, Kulite comes up with a solution." It claims to be the world’s largest supplier of aerospace transducers and points to its ongoing R&D investment, university partnerships, and thousands of custom designs delivered since 1959.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pressure sensors with high proof pressure (5\u2013200\u00d7 overload)", "Pressure ranges 1 PSI to 60,000 PSI (Absolute, Gage, Sealed Gage, Differential)", "Temperature extremes: \u2011320\u202f\u00b0F to 932\u202f\u00b0F continuous operation", "Simultaneous static and dynamic pressure measurements", "Bridge resistance 1,000 ohms typical (350\u201315,000 ohms custom)", "High vibration resistance: 100g peak, sine 10\u20135,000 Hz", "Shunt calibration option", "Unamplified outputs (100 mV typical, 30\u2013300 mV range)", "Amplified outputs (0\u20135 VDC, 0.5\u20135 VDC, 0\u201310 VDC, 4\u201320 mA)", "Special amplified outputs (Potentiometer Replacement, LVDT, Variable Reluctance)", "Custom sensor physical configurations (pressure/electrical connections)", "Submersible transducers/transmitters to 1,100 ft depth", "Pressure switches with single/multiple switched outputs", "Dual and triple redundant sensor designs", "Hermetically sealed gage pressure measurements"], "industries": ["Aerospace/Defense", "Automotive Industry", "Automotive Test/Motorsport", "Space Industry", "Marine", "Process Control", "Military", "Commercial Aircraft", "Oil Exploration", "Coal Mining", "Weather Balloons"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 400 patents in transducer technology", "World''s largest supplier of aerospace transducers", "Custom and stock products for extreme environments (\u2011320\u202f\u00b0F to 932\u202f\u00b0F)", "200,000 sq ft three\u2011building campus with integrated R&D and